Q1 — jQuery Effect Method with Callback Function
The journal asks to create a jQuery effect method using a callback function. It uses hide("slow", function(){...}).     BDNS Journal
Step 1 — Create q1.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>

    <title>Basic jQuery</title>

    <script src="jquery-3.3.1.min.js"></script>

    <script>

        $(document).ready(function(){

            $("button").click(function(){

                $("p").hide("slow", function(){

                    alert("The paragraph is now hidden");

                });

            });

        });

    </script>

</head>

<body>

    <p>Romal:239720</p>
    <p>Welcome to MCC</p>

    <button>Click!</button>

</body>

</html>

Step 2 — Open q1.html
Open it in Chrome.
