Q2 — Get and Set Text Content
The journal uses .text() to get and set the text of an element.     BDNS Journal
Step 1 — Create q2.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>

    <title>Basic jQuery</title>

    <script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>

    <script>

        $(document).ready(function(){

            $("#b1").click(function(){

                var str = $("p").text();

                alert(str);

            });

            $("#b2").click(function(){

                $("p").text("Hello World");

            });

        });

    </script>

</head>

<body>

    <p>Romal Shah:239720</p>
    <p>MongoDB</p>

    <button id="b1">Get</button>
    <button id="b2">Set</button>

</body>

</html>

Step 2 — Open q2.html
Initially:
Romal Shah:239720
MongoDB

[Get] [Set]

Step 3 — Click Get
An alert displays the current text:
Romal Shah:239720 MongoDB

Step 4 — Click Set
The paragraph text changes to:
Hello World

Output
The journal demonstrates the same Get → alert current text and Set → change text to Hello World behavior.     BDNS Journal
